{title: Heritage From The Lord}
{subtitle: Psalms 127:3}
{key: Gm}
{tempo: 70}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Gm] | [Gm] | [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Unless the Lord [Gm]builds the [F]house
Builders [Eb]labor in [Bb]vain
[Dm/A]Unless He [Gm]watches the city
[F]Guardians keep guard in [Eb]vain
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
Rise [Gm]early and stay up late
[F]Bread of anxious toil
But He gives [Eb]sleep
To the one He [Gm]loves
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Children are a heritage from the Lord
The [F]fruit of the womb is a reward
A [Eb]heritage from the Lord
A re[F]ward from on [Gm]high
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Like arrows in the hand of [F]a warrior
So [Eb]are the sons of youth [Bb]
[Dm/A]How [Gm]blessed is the man
Whose [F]quiver is full
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
They [Eb]will not be put to shame
When [F]they contend at the gate
The [Eb]Lord builds your house
The [F]Lord watches your city
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Gm]Children are a heritage from the Lord
The [F]fruit of the womb is a reward
A [Eb]heritage from the Lord
A re[F]ward from on [Gm]high
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Gm] |
| [Gm] | [F] | [Eb] | [F] | ×2

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Gm]Arrows in the hand of [F]a warrior
[Eb]Sons of one's youth [Bb][F/A]
[Gm]Blessed is the man
[F]Full of them [Eb]
{end_of_bridge}

{chorus}

{comment: Outro}
| [Gm] |
| [Gm] | [F] | [Eb] | [F] | ×2
| [Gm] |
